eo_perk_woman_01_pct 0.08 to 0.12, ceo_perk_woman_02_pct 0.08 to 0.15; mining_yield_per_cycle 20 to 30 (one 40-cargo ship hauls 20, so a second ship must still add ore; T156); ships.json dart reworked. See design/proposals/2026-11-05-retune.md. 2026-11-05 v48 (skill-tree-final, economy-designer): NEW skill_LUX_5_event_bonus 0.25, skill_MIL_2_batches 1, skill_LUX_6_batch_bonus 1, skill_BIO_3_stock_cap 0.30. RETUNED skill_MIL_5_hit 0.18 to 0.35, skill_MIL_5_cycles 3 to 4, skill_MIL_6_event_cut 0.5 to 0.35, skill_LUX_7_hit 0.18 to 0.30, skill_LUX_7_cycles 5 to 8, skill_MIN_7_strength_cut 0.1 to 0.2, skill_BIO_7_strength_cut 0.1 to 0.15. REMOVED unused skill_size_s, skill_size_m, skill_MIL_3_route_units, skill_MIL_4_price, skill_LUX_1_price, skill_LUX_6_price, skill_BIO_1_order_units. 2026-11-05 v47 (ship-ceo-data, economy-designer): NEW keys only: ceo_step_haggling 0.008, ceo_step_thrift 0.02, ceo_step_nerve 0.04, upkeep_floor 0.5, ceo_perk_<id>_* (4 perks). Ship modifiers live in data/ships.json. 2026-11-05 v46 (balance-retune, economy-designer, overnight QA): maintenance 45 to 40; nothing else changed (bot_2_lux_growth, sweep_share_pct, ship_cap tested and rejected, see qa/reports/2026-11-05-balance-retune.md). 2026-11-04 v45 (ship-cap-6, economy-designer, owner request): ship_cap 5 to 6; nothing else changed. 2026-11-04 v44 (storage-income-2000, economy-designer, owner request): earn_storage_income 3000 to 2000 (Space Storage income line); nothing else changed. 2026-11-04 v43 (storage-no-cycle-gate, gameplay-programmer, owner request): REMOVED key earn_storage_cycles; Space Storage now needs only earn_storage_income (3000, PLACEHOLDER). 2026-11-03 v42 (chain-min-cycle, gameplay-programmer): NEW key chain_min_cycle 6 (no chain step fires before this cycle; owner: well after the tutorial and first routes, sensible range 5-7, PLACEHOLDER, economy designer owns the final value). Cause: early share_pct triggers (B1 any-of skill or share 30) passed at cycle 2 with tiny early rival values. 2026-11-03 v41 (storage-earned-lock, gameplay-programmer): NEW keys earn_storage_cycles 5 and earn_storage_income 3000 (Space Storage FND_STORAGE can be learned only at cycle >= 5 AND cumulative gross trade income >= 3000; PLACEHOLDER for the economy designer: about 2 cycles of one-system net income, 1.4 start cash). 2026-11-03 v40 (endings-retune-r2, economy-designer): per-market rival strengths and growth (all bots) x1.4 mil, x2.6 lux, x1.8 min, x1.25 bio on top of v39 (bot_scale stays 0.22); win_earliest_cycle 22 to 23. Reason: v39 gave the focused QA bot 100 pct wins at 57-88 pct share; now about 85-90 pct, median cycle 26-29, spread and mining_focus no longer win. 2026-11-03 v39 (endings-retune, economy-designer): bot_scale 0.85 to 0.22; bot_*_bio_strength/growth x0.65, bot_*_min_strength/growth x0.4 (mil and lux unchanged relative); win_earliest_cycle 20 to 22. Reason: real bot player volume is about 700 bv a cycle (3 ships, energy or food lanes, no crafting) against the 2.7-4k paper ramp, so rivals at 0.85 left a 5 pct share and END_SWEPT at c27. With these numbers decent --no-permit wins mil c26, bio c26, mining_focus min c26-28; default permit-2 bot and spread still collapse (code gaps in the handoff). 2026-11-03 v38 (chain-data, economy-designer): NEW keys only for event chains: chain_min_gap, dir_* rules (cap 14, echo 1.25, swing 1.5, swing_min_abs 25), win_gate_cycle 38, event_hit_strength_*/growth_*/tier sizes (economy 8.1; old event_hit_s/m/l kept, L 0.2 vs 0.18 differs), and chain_<STEP>_<a|b>_* values for the 56 options (data/chains.json). 2026-11-03 v37 (skills-core, gameplay-programmer): REMOVED old tree keys (skill_cost_A1..C4/M1/M2/F1, skill_A2_capacity, skill_C4_permit_discount, skill_A4_route_units, skill_B2_order_units, skill_B3_margin, skill_A5_upkeep); NEW ending_second_market_pct 0.25 (core 6: a second market over 25% adds an ending flavour line); applied economy retunes skill_points_route 1, skill_points_system 2, permit_points_2 2, permit_points_3 2. 2026-11-03 v36 (skill-data, economy-designer): NEW keys only for the four market trees (nothing removed; old A/B/C/M/F keys stay until the code that reads them is removed): skill_cost_<id> for 3 Foundations + 28 nodes, tech_goal_2/4/6 9/18/12 (R1), skill_points_share_20/35 1/2, skill_size_s/m/l 0.08/0.15/0.30, per-node skill_<NODE>_<what> values (economy section 5), workshop_build_cost 900, workshop_batches_per_cycle 1, size_slots_M/L, <good>_batch_out, event_pct for the 11 new goods. Bot interaction numbers: embargo every 8 cycles for 3 (skill_MIL_5_*), guild seal 5 cycles once per run (skill_LUX_7_*), capstone growth x0.5. Node graph: data/skills.json; goods: data/goods.json. 2026-11-03 v35 (bot-hooks, gameplay-programmer): NEW keys event_hit_s 0.05, event_hit_m 0.10, event_hit_l 0.20 (size of an event hit on a bot, S/M/L as a fraction; PLACEHOLDERS, economy-designer owns the values). 2026-11-03 v34 (market-foundation, gameplay-programmer): REMOVED win_cycle and win_cash (the old cash goal is gone; run length is win_cycle_markets 40). 2026-11-03 v33 (market-keys, economy-designer): NEW keys only for Four Markets Goal 2 (share, win, sweep, overhead, bots, rescue_max, win_cycle_markets 40); nothing removed, win_cycle and win_cash unchanged. 2026-11-03 v32 (passability, economy-designer): trip_cost 90 to 60, maintenance 60 to 45 (fixed cost of one route 110 to 80; the real game needs working capital of fixed cost plus stock per route, and at 110 five routes held 550 before any Buy, which stalled bot runs at cash 144-300); win_cash 12500 to 14000 (re-centres sim decent median at 24). Cause of sim vs bot gap: the sim decent buys permit 2 (C1 + 600) at cycle 10-13, the bot default never does and stays in system 1 (about 570 net per cycle, ends 3081 median); stalls need a code fix (see handoff). 2026-11-03 v31 (dead-planet-rebalance, economy-designer): fabric_build_cost 1000 to 600 (dead worlds open at cycle 15, first plate cycle 16; at 100 net per batch 1000 repays by cycle 26, after the typical win 22-27; 600 repays in 6 cycles, 8 batches by cycle 23); dead_shore_cost 400 to 250 and dead_ore_loss_pct 0.3 to 0.4 (expected ore loss for one nullglass ship over 3 cycles ~230, shore up priced just above it); dead_income_cut 0.25 to 0.2, dead_income_boost 0.25 to 0.3 (race also adds danger, so the boost must outpay the cut); null_core_build_cost 2000 to 250 and null_core_in_nullglass 1 to 2 (core saves 45 per cycle on a 90 trip, total cost ~430 with inputs, payback ~10 cycles); null_core_in_plate 1, null_core_max 1, null_core_trip_mult 0.5, dead_ore_loss_chance 0.5, dead_ore_loss_cycles 3, dead_income_cycles 3 kept. Sim does not model dead worlds: decent unchanged. 2026-11-03 v31 (dead-planets-audit, gameplay-programmer): NEW keys. dead_unlock_cycle 15 (owner: dead worlds reachable only from cycle 15). Null Core, all PLACEHOLDERS for the economy designer: null_core_in_plate 1, null_core_in_nullglass 1, null_core_build_cost 2000, null_core_max 1 (owner rule: one per run), null_core_trip_mult 0.5 (design: the fitted ship's trips cost half). No existing value changed. 2026-11-03 v30 (dead-effects, gameplay-programmer): NEW keys only, all PLACEHOLDERS for the economy designer to set: dead_shore_cost 400 (EV32 shore up, = debris_clear_fee), dead_ore_loss_chance 0.5 (= asteroid_decline_bad_odds), dead_ore_loss_pct 0.3 (share of a load lost, = pirate_volume_penalty), dead_ore_loss_cycles 3 and dead_income_cycles 3 (= event_price_cycles), dead_income_cut 0.25 and dead_income_boost 0.25 (= debris_route_penalty); no existing value changed. 2026-11-02 v29 (dead-planet-economy r2, QA blocker: C3 not affordable with the chain): skill_cost_M1 2 to 1, skill_cost_M2 3 to 2, skill_cost_F1 3 to 2. Chain B1+A1+C1+C2+C3+M1+M2+F1 = 1+1+1+1+2+1+2+2 = 11 points, plus permit_points_2 3 = 14 (was 17); at full_ref 0.7 points a cycle that is cycle 20 (was 24). 2026-11-02 v28 (dead-planet-economy): fabric_build_cost 1500 to 1000 (plate margin 100 per batch vs mining cost 20, payback 10 cycles). 2026-11-02 v27 (fabric): fabric_build_cost 1500 (spec design/proposals/2026-11-02-dead-planets.md section 4, point 2: one-time, credits allowed, skill-point rule does not apply); fabric_in_dross 2, fabric_in_nullglass 1, fabric_out_plate 1, fabric_batches_per_cycle 1 (task brief recipe: 2 dross + 1 nullglass -> 1 plate); plate_buy 60 and plate_sell 48 on planet_1 in data/planets.json are PLACEHOLDERS for the economy designer. 2026-11-02 v26 (dead-planets, design/proposals/2026-11-02-dead-planets.md): skill_cost_M1 2, skill_cost_M2 3, skill_cost_F1 3 (spec section 3); dead_danger_max 5 and dead_danger_rise 1 per mining cycle (task brief: danger 0 to 5, +1 a cycle); dead_follow_cycles 4 (spec section 5 proposal, default for follow-up events). No existing value changed. 2026-11-02 v25 (alpha-economy-r2, QA round 1 decent 1 of 8): ship_cap 6 to 5, win_cash 11500 to 12500. Mirror 100 seeds: decent 98% median 26, always_expand 65%, sloppy/never_expand 0%, cash row3 276, ship3 median 10. Buy gate tested in sim (buy_gate): gate 300-500 makes always_expand win 99-100% at cap 6 and 0% at cap 24, so the cap stays the limiter. 2026-11-02 v24 (alpha-economy, tools/sim.py --settle mirrors settle + reserve + bot): ship_cap 24 to 6, win_cash 8500 to 11500, trip_cost 95 to 90. With the cash reserve the naive QA bots buy a ship whenever cash >= price, so cash after each buy is ~0 and N routes x fixed cost starve every Buy; 24 ships never fund. Cap 6 keeps cash for working capital; win_cash 11500 keeps one ship + permit (ends ~10100) losing; trip 90 brings ship 3 from cycle 13 to 10. Mirror 400 seeds: decent 91% median 26 (21-30), mining_focus 95% median 25, always_expand 33% median 26, sloppy/never_expand/never_expand+permit 0%. 2026-11-02 v23 (frost-event, owner feedback): event_pct_energy 0.35 added (was default event_price_pct 0.2); energy price events only, sim decent median 22 unchanged. 2026-11-02 v22 (reserve-rebalance): starting_credits 1800 to 2100 (QA v4: cash reserve delayed ship 3 from cycle 3 to 7-10, 0 of 8 wins; +300 float restores early tempo; sim decent 98% median 23). 2026-11-02 v21 (T153, goal trade-goods-asteroid-mining): new goods and mining keys, template values (owner confirms in T161). 2026-11-02 v20: N3 Mixed load keys bundle_bonus_pct 0.05, bundle_bonus_cap 150 added (owner approved). 2026-11-02 v19: upgrade_cost 600 to 900 (T144: route upgrade level 2 offered on a full lane; at 600 decent no-skill win moves to cycle 23, below target; 900 keeps median 26). 2026-11-01 v18: ship_price 1000 to 900 (pacing retune: permit path median 26, natural decent 29/30). 2026-10-31 v17: skill-tree r2: A5 upkeep 0.2 to 0.3 (QA: 0 cycles after A4). 2026-10-31 v16: skill-tree r1: A4 0.15 to 0.125, A5 0.3 to 0.2, B3 0.12 to 0.08 (sim: each ~2-3 cycles faster if owned from start, was 3-4). 2026-10-31 v15: permit_2_cost 1000 to 600. Only Full-tier runs buy the permit, so base play is unchanged. Bot evidence: Full Research 4/4, Full Logistics 4/4, Full Expansion 6/8, full tree 7/8 (was 0/4 Research, 1/4 tree, with bot lane and ship bugs). Owner and economy designer to confirm. 2026-10-31 v14: skill_A2_capacity 0.5 and skill_C4_permit_discount 0.2 added (template values, owner and economy designer to confirm). 2026-10-28 v13: A3 and hauler keys removed. v12: planet_to_space_rate 3 to 1 (QA A1 leak). v11: added debris, shield, pirate, asteroid keys (owner ideas 1,3,5). Template values marked in handoff.",
